{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
  "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When a prisoner wins a civil rights\ncase and he's awarded damages and he's awarded\nattorney's fees, the prisoner himself has to\npay part of the fees out of the damages\njudgment. The statute at issue in this case\nspecifies the size of the prisoner's share.\nThis is what the statute says: \"A portion of\nthe judgment (not to exceed 25 percent) shall\nbe applied to satisfy the amount of attorney's\nfees.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Your adversary\npoints to a number of statutes that use the\nverb \"to satisfy\" -- or I guess not the verb,\nbut the proposition \"to satisfy\" -- to refer to\nthe complete fulfillment of an obligation. How\ndo you distinguish those examples?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district courts have been -- in\ndeciding on the appropriate share for the\nplaintiff to pay, the district courts have been\nconsidering the extent to which making the\ndefendant pay a greater share will deter future\nmisconduct by prison guards, and the extent to\nwhich making the plaintiff pay a greater share\nwill deter prisoners with meritorious claims\nfrom filing suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the award of attorney's fees is\ngreater than 25 percent of the judgment, the excess shall be paid by the defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why? Where do you get that from? Where in the -- anywhere is that said, is that discussed, is that indicated in the -- in this section at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LEGNER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEGNER: Sure, Your Honor. We get that from a variety of sources. The first is the statute's text. Congress said that the district court shall apply a portion of the judgment to satisfy -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: No, it says a portion of the judgment. So it doesn't say all of the judgment. It -- it doesn't say the judgment shall be applied to satisfy the amount of attorney's fees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Legner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress explicitly moved away from the operation of Section 1988. And so it moved away from the broad or wide fee shifting or complete fee shifting under Section 1988 to something else. And in -- in so moving, it moved towards the American rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can I ask about something else, which is we've made the American rule the presumption, but I come at it, why aren't we looking at the discretionary rule of 1988?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1067",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-46b45685fd88-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
